%% FleetOS — 3-layer auth defense (MASTER_PLAN.md Phase 3).
%% The point of this diagram: the proxy is UX-only. Every layer below it
%% independently re-checks the session, on the assumption the layer above
%% could have been bypassed (this is the direct fix for CVE-2025-29927 —
%% a real middleware-authorization-bypass vulnerability).
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as Browser
    participant Px as proxy.ts (edge)
    participant SA as Server Action / Route Handler
    participant Sess as session.ts
    participant DB as Postgres (RLS, Phase 6+)

    U->>Px: Request /dashboard/vessels
    Note over Px: Redirect-only.<br/>NOT the real security boundary.
    alt no session cookie
        Px-->>U: 302 redirect to /login
    else session cookie present
        Px->>SA: forward request
        Note over SA: Independently verifies the session -<br/>never trusts that the proxy already checked.
        SA->>Sess: validateSession(cookie)
        alt session invalid/expired
            Sess-->>SA: null
            SA-->>U: redirect /login (defense-in-depth,<br/>not relying on the proxy alone)
        else session valid
            Sess-->>SA: { userId, role }
            Note over SA: Phase 6: role check against WRITE_ROLES<br/>before any write
            SA->>DB: query/mutate (RLS policy re-enforces<br/>the same scoping at the DB layer)
            DB-->>SA: result
            SA-->>U: response
        end
    end
